# Pearl Product Stress Standard

Canonical detail: `docs/pearl-stress-standard.md`. Showcase catalog: `docs/pearl-showcase-flows.md`. Gap audit: `docs/pearl-stress-clueless-gap-audit.md`. Coverage: `docs/pearl-stress-coverage.md`.

**Master harness:** `npm run stress:clueless` → `scripts/pearl-clueless-stress.mjs` (hard-fail). Also: `npm run stress:pearl` (core + gaps; must obey the same integrity rules).

Whenever you audit, stress, review, or claim completion for **any** new or existing feature/flow:

1. Evaluate as the **Clueless First-Time Persona** only — hyper-clueless: no jargon, no “they should know to say merge,” no reading source code, no mode pickers, no tour walls.
2. Run the headed clueless/showcase harness against this standard — not unit tests alone.
3. Cover all lenses in the standard doc plus every catalogued showcase flow in `docs/pearl-showcase-flows.md`.
4. Prefer fixing broken claimed paths over documenting them as acceptable.
5. Never claim production-ready / perfect / fully working / state of the art unless evidence supports that exact claim. State credential, mic, extension, and auth gaps explicitly.

## Hard fails

Navigation traps, inaccessible primary action, fake Done, silent data loss/dupes, companion fake success, white-dot Pearl fallback, user-facing "orb", gauntlet >5 without clear refuse, Studio not M→F→L when structure exists, **confusion budget >1 unexplained click** to start talking, topic-create accepted as generic `New pearl · …`, chat success without **world-visible** titled artifact.

## Clueless First-Time Persona (only acceptable UX evaluator)

- Lands cold; finds Talk without hunting.
- Types naive natural language a novice would invent.
- Must **see** the world change (Reef/gauntlet/Studio label readable in screenshot).
- Multi-step continuity without harness reset: create → rename → edit → wear → merge.
- 390px phone-first is a primary journey, not an afterthought.

## World-state visibility

Every successful mutation must be findable on screen by a title/label a human can read in the screenshot. Storage/chat alone is insufficient.

## No privileged shortcuts in journeys

`__lensOrbRuntime.run` / `.execute` and `localStorage` seeding are allowed only in **isolated unit tests** — never as the pass criterion for `stress:clueless` / Companion UX journeys.

## Intent binding

Create “about X” must yield a pearl whose visible title clearly relates to X — not generic `New pearl · stamp`, not Untitled, not orb.

## Visual-first gate (equal weight to world-state)

For **every** meaningful state in showcase/clueless flows:

1. Screenshot full viewport (+ chat dock crop when relevant).
2. **Read the actual PNG** with the image Read tool (look at pixels — not DOM heuristics alone).
3. Write a human critique: hierarchy, clutter, stacking, invisible controls, contrast, mystery objects, “would a clueless user find the next action in &lt;3 seconds?”
4. **FAIL** if anything critical is invisible, occluded, low-contrast to unreadability, stacked illegibly, or looks broken — **even if DOM asserts and runtime effects passed**.
5. Functional-only green without visual pass = **invalid harness lie**.

**Invisible = Fail. Bot-only reachable = Fail.**

## Screenshot veto

Human **Read** of real PNGs **must** fail the suite when the above breaks. Document critiques that reference what was **seen** in images (not boilerplate).

## Anti-lie checklist (every PR / stress run)

- [ ] No runtime.execute/run as journey pass
- [ ] No force:true on primary controls
- [ ] No seed-as-pass / pearls[0] fallback for create identity
- [ ] No Untitled / user-facing orb / topic-create as generic New pearl
- [ ] Visible Reef/gauntlet title for every successful mutation
- [ ] Talk→GO only for Companion UX; confusion budget ≤1
- [ ] Continuity without harness reset for marathon flow
- [ ] Human Read veto recorded for primary PNGs
- [ ] Skipped env rows never counted in pass totals
- [ ] Exact blocker when vague — never dead air

Minimum valid create path: GO hit-test → user echo → status → companion reply → **visible** Reef pearl with intent-related human title → reload findability. See `docs/pearl-stress-standard.md`.
